## 31.6 Sparklines: gtExtras Method

Before we can prepare the sales report by product by using gtExtras
functions, the code chunk below will be used to prepare the data.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true" code-summary="Show the code"}
report <- coffeechain %>%
  mutate(Year = year(Date)) %>%
  filter(Year == "2013") %>%
  mutate (Month = month(Date,
                        label = TRUE,
                        abbr = TRUE)) %>%
  group_by(Product, Month) %>%
  summarise(Sales = sum(Sales)) %>%
  ungroup()
```
:::


It is important to note that one of the requirements of gtExtras
functions is that almost exclusively they require you to pass data.frame
with list columns. In view of this, the code chunk below will be used to
convert the report data.frame into list columns.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true" code-summary="Show the code"}
report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarize('Monthly Sales' = list(Sales),
            .groups = "drop")
```

